From cb85168d2694e9c36d00ce1407882c88fadd4f59 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adrian Vovk <adrianvovk@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Jun 2025 15:23:02 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 06/51] Split -binary into -leader and -service

Now gnome-session (the shell script) launches the gnome-session-leader,
which talks to systemd over IPC to launch the session. Part of the
session is gnome-session-service (which is what used to be
gnome-session-binary in --systemd-service mode)

There is now no more fallback functionality from systemd startup to the
legacy builtin session. If systemd startup fails, the session doesn't
start.
