From 80f1b7ba665d1e8682a8559c64855621c53d2db9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adrian Vovk <adrianvovk@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Jun 2025 21:04:28 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 08/51] leader: Replace leader shell script with C code

Before, we were doing a weird mix & match: some environment variables
were set directly in the leader, others were set in the shell script and
the leader inherited them. This commit reconciles this

Why move everything into C instead of moving more things out to shell?
Because shell is fragile. Just look at the example where you need to
pass `G_MESSAGES_DEBUG=''` to the gsettings invocation to make sure you
don't get an environment variable full of nonsense. C is just easier to
reason about, there's no bashisms to consider, etc
