From 8f060e68612e3310c729777b4ff942ed8f30266b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adrian Vovk <adrianvovk@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Jun 2025 19:23:43 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 10/51] manager: Cut down the number of phases

STARTUP: This phase was active while gnome-session started the dbus
session bus. But now the user session bus is running before
gnome-session even launches.

EARLY_INIT: This phase was only used by the
gnome-initial-setup-copy-worker, which is now managed by systemd

PRE_DISPLAY_SERVER: This phase was reserved for starting gnome-keyring,
but gnome-keyring is actually started by PAM way before gnome-session is
launched

DISPLAY_SERVER: This phase was used to launch gnome-shell. This is also
managed by systemd nowadays

WINDOW_MANAGER, PANEL, DESKTOP: These distinctions predate Wayland and
gnome-shell. These features are now built directly into the display
