From 3791d8938ac39a38386c315304814e08b8cedeae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adrian Vovk <adrianvovk@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Jun 2025 18:09:41 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 43/51] manager: Cleanup phase timeouts

We were only ever using the query_timeout in PHASE_QUERY_END_SESSION,
and the phase_timeout in PHASE_END_SESSION. Since these don't overlap,
we can use the same timeout.

We also adjust the PHASE_END_SESSION timeout back down to 10 seconds,
which is the documented time limit that apps have to respond. I did a
bit of git archaeology: the timeout was originally 10 seconds, but
session _startup_ phases also had a 10 second timeout. Thus, the
timeouts shared one #define. Eventually, the startup timeouts increased
to 30 seconds then to 90 (to deal with live media and slow drives), and
simply nobody noticed that this changed the timeout of PHASE_END_SESSION
to 90 seconds as well.
---
 gnome-session/gsm-manager.c | 57 +++++++++----------------------------
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 43 deletions(-)

diff --git a/gnome-session/gsm-manager.c b/gnome-session/gsm-manager.c
index a77f53b5..b261343f 100644
--- a/gnome-session/gsm-manager.c
+++ b/gnome-session/gsm-manager.c
@@ -57,16 +57,6 @@
